    "status": "present",
    "value": "Let dp[i][j] be the number of distinct non-empty palindromic subsequences inside s[i..j]. If s[i] != s[j], no palindrome uses both ends, so dp[i][j] = dp[i+1][j] + dp[i][j-1] - dp[i+1][j-1] by inclusion-exclusion. If s[i] == s[j] = x, every palindrome of the inside either stays as it is or gets wrapped as x...x, giving 2*dp[i+1][j-1], plus the new strings x and xx unless they already exist inside. Let low be the first x strictly inside and high the last. No x inside: add 2 (x and xx). Exactly one x inside: add 1 (only xx is new). Two or more: x and xx already exist, and the palindromes strictly between low and high were wrapped twice, so subtract dp[low+1][high-1]."
  },
